    {model:'Large-Capacity Filters',type:'Filter',pdf:[92,93],aliases:['LCRBY100D','LCRBY150S','LCRBY150D','LCRBY200S','LCRBY200D'],facts:['1 in disc-only maximum 26 gpm; 1.5 in screen/disc maximum 62 gpm; 2 in screen/disc maximum 110 gpm.','Maximum pressure 116 psi (8 bar), temperature 140°F (60°C); 120 mesh (130 micron) filtration and NPT inlet/outlet.','Install downstream of valve to avoid constant pressure.','Source inconsistency: page 93 provides 1 in screen-filter loss values although page 92 says screen unavailable in 1 in model; no 1 in screen product inferred.']},
    {model:'Large-Capacity Replacement Filters',type:'Irrigation Accessory',pdf:[91,92],aliases:['LGFC120MS','LGFC120MD'],facts:['Replacement 120 mesh screen (MS) or disc (MD) elements listed for 1.5–2 in filters and commercial control-zone kits.']},
    {model:'ESP-9V Battery-Operated Controller',type:'Field Controller',pdf:[94,94],aliases:['ESP9V1','ESP9V2','ESP9V4','ESP9V6','ESP9V1SOL','ESP9VDVKIT','K80920','Hunter 458700','Irritrol DCL','Toro DCLS-P'],facts:['1/2/4/6-zone models; one-zone with 9 V solenoid or one-zone with 1 in slip DV valve kits explicitly listed.','IP68 waterproof case, sensor input/bypass, six start times per zone, one valve irrigating at a time; master valve/pump-start circuit only on multi-zone units.','One 9 V alkaline battery approximately one year, two approximately two years under catalog assumptions.','Compatible latching-solenoid identifiers Rain Bird K80920, Hunter 458700, Irritrol DCL, Toro DCLS-P; these are compatibility references, not new third-party product specifications.']},
    {model:'9VMOUNT',type:'Irrigation Accessory',pdf:[94,94],aliases:['ESP-9V Wall-Mount Kit'],facts:['Optional wall-mount kit for ESP-9V controller.']},
    {model:'ESP-BAT-BT Bluetooth Battery-Operated Controller',type:'Field Controller',pdf:[95,95],aliases:['ESPBAT-BT1','ESPBAT-BT2','ESPBAT-BT4','ESPBAT-BT6','BAT-BT','Rain Bird App'],facts:['1/2/4/6-station models, dedicated master-valve/pump output on all models; IP68 certification.','Runtime 7 seconds–9 hours in 1-second increments, up to 18 hours with 200% seasonal adjustment; Cycle and Soak down to 7 seconds.','Catalog battery-life estimate 3–5 years; retains irrigation program during replacement.','Android/iOS app supports device sharing, saved local programs and offline edits synchronized when back in Bluetooth range; offline app is not remote live control.','All BAT-BT controllers require a 9 V DC latching valve solenoid.']},
    {model:'TBOSPSOL Potted Latching Solenoid',type:'Irrigation Accessory',pdf:[95,95],aliases:['TBOSPSOL','9-Volt Potted DC Latching Solenoid'],facts:['9 V potted DC latching solenoid, listed with BAT-BT compatibility for DV/DVF/ASVF/PGA/PEB/PESB/EFB-CP/BPE/BPES valves.']},
    {model:'Conversion Factors, Equivalents and Formulas',type:'Technical Reference',pdf:[96,96],aliases:['unit conversion','area','volume','head','pressure','power','temperature'],facts:['Reference covers area, length, volume, mass, pressure, flow, power and temperature conversions.','US gallon 3.785 L; acre 43,560 ft²; head 2.31 ft per psi; horsepower 746 W; Celsius=(Fahrenheit−32)×5/9.','Some legacy rounded conversion factors differ from modern exact values; use consistent units rather than transcribing every rounded chart number.']},
    {model:'Precipitation and Runtime Design Formulas',type:'Technical Reference',pdf:[97,97],aliases:['precipitation rate','square spacing','triangular spacing','single row','runtime'],facts:['Square PR (in/hr)=96.3×Q(gpm)×360/[S(ft)²×arc(degrees)]; triangular PR adds 0.866 to denominator.','Single-row PR=96.3×Q/[S×0.8×throw diameter], with distances in feet.','Runtime (minutes)=desired application (inches)×60/PR(in/hr).','These geometric formulas assume the specified spacing and arc and do not replace measured distribution uniformity or wind-adjusted design.']},
    {model:'Hydraulic and Power Formulas',type:'Technical Reference',pdf:[97,97],aliases:['velocity','water horsepower','brake horsepower','TDH','affinity laws','Ohm law','kVA','power factor'],facts:['Velocity (ft/s)=0.480×Q(gpm)/ID(in)².','Water HP=Q(gpm)×TDH(ft)/3960; brake HP divides by pump efficiency expressed as a fraction.','Pump affinity: flow follows speed ratio, pressure its square, power its cube under affinity-law assumptions.','Ohm law V=IR; apparent power kVA=V×I/1000 single-phase or 1.732×V×I/1000 three-phase.','AC real-power/current formulas additionally require power factor and motor efficiency where appropriate; simple watts/volts is not a universal AC motor-sizing rule.']},
    {model:'Wire Resistance and Motor Full-Load Amperage',type:'Technical Reference',pdf:[98,98],aliases:['FLA','horsepower to kilowatts','NFPA 70','National Electric Code','VFD'],facts:['Wire resistance table distinguishes gauge, solid/stranded conductor and temperature, citing 2008 NEC chapter 9 table 8.','Designer must use resistance appropriate to project temperature/application; this catalog is not a substitute for current electrical code.','Catalog FLA guidance: increase 230 V table current by 10% for 208 V; multiply nominal FLA by 1.24 for VFD motor estimate.','Station estimate uses largest load×1.25 plus remaining component FLAs; final sizing requires actual equipment and applicable code.']},
    {model:'Pressure, Filtration and Intake Sizing Tables',type:'Technical Reference',pdf:[99,99],aliases:['micron to mesh','intake pipe sizing','lake intake box screen','wet well open area'],facts:['Reference tables convert pressure/head and mesh/micron openings and size intake pipes, lake intake screens and wet wells by flow.','Lake-intake screen sizing based on screen velocity below 0.5 ft/s; wet-well selection depends on shape and number of vertical turbines.','Use source table and manufacturer selection for flows/configurations outside tabulated range; do not treat mesh number alone as a unique opening for all screen constructions.']},
    {model:'HDPE Pipe Velocity and Friction Reference',type:'Technical Reference',pdf:[100,101],aliases:['PE 4710','IPS','HDPE','DR 13.5','161 psi','C=150'],facts:['Tables for PE 4710 IPS HDPE DR 13.5, labeled 161 psi; velocity ft/s and friction loss psi/100 ft, C=150.','Nominal sizes 2–18 in use listed actual inside diameters; continuation covers higher flows.','Shaded velocities require caution; table friction is not an installation pressure rating or allowable surge limit.']},
    {model:'Class 200 PVC Pipe Velocity and Friction Reference',type:'Technical Reference',pdf:[102,103],aliases:['SDR 21','Class 200 PVC','C=150'],facts:['SDR 21 Class 200 PVC tables use velocity ft/s and friction loss psi/100 ft with C=150.','Nominal 1–12 in sizes use listed actual inside diameters; continuation covers higher flows.','Use caution at shaded velocities; nominal pipe size is not its hydraulic inside diameter.']},
    {model:'IC System Wire Path Design Reference',type:'Technical Reference',pdf:[104,104],aliases:['ICS Wire Path','MAXI','14 AWG','12 AWG','10 AWG','2.5 mm²','4.0 mm²','6.0 mm²'],facts:['Gauge selection tables relate ICM count to trunk length in feet or meters; trunk is longest single wire run, not total sum of branches.','Branches may be added but do not increase maximum ICM count per path.','Catalog recommends balancing paths and leaving room below full 750-ICM capacity for expansion and sensors.','Blank cells provide no design approval; IC-IN weighting and grounding requirements still apply.']},
    {model:'Water Velocity Reference',type:'Technical Reference',pdf:[105,105],aliases:['internal pipe diameter','mainline','wet-well intake'],facts:['Velocity chart uses actual internal pipe diameter, not nominal size.','Catalog standard-practice targets: mainline below 5 ft/s, wet-well intake below 1.5 ft/s; confirm class/type-specific inside diameter.']},
    {model:'Controller Power Wiring Sizing Worksheet',type:'Technical Reference',pdf:[106,106],aliases:['PAR+ES power wiring','PAR+ES LINK with Radio','PAR+ES SAT Decoder','PAR+ES SAT Decoder LINK with Radio'],facts:['Input-current table covers four controller/radio configurations, idle and active solenoid counts.','Based on 117 VAC input; catalog says use 50% of listed current for 220/240 VAC inputs.','Includes master valve; decoder assumptions consider 72 installed decoders; simultaneous limits 16 at 60 Hz or 12 at 50 Hz.','Do not substitute output solenoid current for controller supply-circuit current.']},
    {model:'752 VIH Low-Flow Maximum Inlet Pressure',type:'Technical Reference',pdf:[107,107],aliases:['752 #18 Beige','752 #20 Gray','752 #22 Red','752 #24 Plum','752 #26 Lt. Green','70 psi case','80 psi case'],facts:['Image-verified limits for 70/80 psi cases respectively: #18 90/115 psi; #20 105/130 psi; #22/#24/#26 115/130 psi.','These nozzle-specific inlet limits override the generic 150 psi E/IC family ceiling for listed low-flow configurations.']},
    {model:'Customer Satisfaction and Warranty Policy',type:'Support Service',pdf:[108,108],aliases:['Golf Warranty','Pump Station Warranty','LINK Radios'],facts:['Golf rotors three years, extended to five with concurrently installed Rain Bird swing joints and proof; golf controllers/satellites one year and LINK radios three years.','Pump station manufacturing-defect policy three years from startup, not beyond forty months from purchase; authorized startup/service and maintenance conditions apply, labor coverage not beyond one year from startup.','Not comprehensive legal terms; lightning/flooding exclusions and jurisdictional limitations apply in source.','Source inconsistency: valve-box product page 58 states five years while golf-policy page 108 lists valve boxes with three-year products; confirm applicable warranty.','Warranty-only mentions of other landscape/agricultural products are not evidence of full product specifications in this golf catalog.']},
    {model:'Rain Bird Technical Services',type:'Support Service',pdf:[110,110],aliases:['GSP-XPRT','Golf Technical Services'],facts:['US/Canada technical-services contact (866) 477-9778, presented as (866) GSP-XPRT.','Back cover copyright 2026, print mark 7/26 and document code D31245YEO corroborate 2026–2027 cover edition.']},
    {model:'IC Interface',type:'Central Control',pdf:[28,28],aliases:['ICI','Output Driver Board'],facts:['IC System specification describes 3,000 ICMs per IC Interface, 1,500 per output driver board and 750 per wire path.','Input nominal ranges: 98–132 VAC for 115 VAC, 208–255 VAC for 220–240 VAC and 91–110 VAC for 100 VAC.','Do not apply legacy central maximum-interface counts to CirrusPRO without its separate ICI+ guidance.']},
    {model:'Legacy Central Compatibility Reference',type:'Technical Reference',pdf:[28,42],aliases:['Cirrus','Nimbus','Nimbus II','Stratus II','StratusLT','Smart Pump','Smart Weather','Minimum ET','MI Series Mobile Controller'],facts:['Legacy central names appear in IC/decoder compatibility and interface-limit discussions, not separate current central-product specification sections.','Page 28 lists Cirrus twelve interfaces/48 paths, Nimbus eight/32, Stratus II two/eight and StratusLT one/one; capacities are central-specific.','ICI+ hybrid compatibility references Cirrus version 8.1 or higher and Nimbus II/Stratus variants; CirrusPRO is described separately.']},
    {model:'952LT Rotor Accessories',type:'Irrigation Accessory',pdf:[14,14],aliases:['Green Rubber Cover','Purple Rubber Cover','Low Angle Nozzle Housing'],facts:['Optional green/purple rubber replacement cover and low-angle nozzle housing explicitly listed for 952LT.','Sod cup kit is indexed separately; no accessory order part number supplied on this page.']}
